      "sample_index": 2,
      "text": "To solve the problem, we need to find the volumes of the two cubes and then determine the ratio of these volumes.\n\n1. **Find the volume of the cube with an edge length of 6 inches:**\n\n   The formula for the volume \\( V \\) of a cube with edge length \\( s \\) is:\n   \\[\n   V = s^3\n   \\]\n\n   For a cube with edge length 6 inches:\n   \\[\n   V_1 = 6^3 = 6 \\times 6 \\times 6 = 216 \\text{ cubic inches}\n   \\]\n\n2. **Find the volume of the cube with an edge length of 1 foot:**\n\n   First, convert the edge length from feet to inches. Since there are 12 inches in a foot:\n   \\[\n   1 \\text{ foot} = 12 \\text{ inches}\n   \\]\n\n   Now, find the volume using the same formula:\n   \\[\n   V_2 = 12^3 = 12 \\times 12 \\times 12 = 144 \\text{ cubic inches}\n   \\]\n\n3. **Find the ratio of the volumes:**\n\n   The ratio of the volume of the first cube to the volume of the second cube is:\n   \\[\n   \\text{Ratio} = \\frac{V_1}{V_2} = \\frac{216}{144}\n   \\]\n\n4. **Simplify the fraction:**\n\n   To simplify \\(\\frac{216}{144}\\), we find the greatest common divisor (GCD) of 216 and 144. The GCD of 216 and 144 is 72.\n\n   Divide both the numerator and the denominator by their GCD:\n   \\[\n   \\frac{216 \\div 72}{144 \\div 72} = \\frac{3}{2}\n   \\]\n\nTherefore, the ratio of the volume of the cube with an edge length of 6 inches to the volume of the cube with an edge length of 1 foot is \\(\\boxed{\\frac{3}{2}}\\).",
